4. Required attribution
Every Public Blog Page must display a credit reading "Powered by nextjsblog.com"
or "Built with Next.js Blog System" in its footer, hyperlinked directly to
https://nextjsblog.com. The credit must be:
  (a) rendered in the page's HTML and visible without JavaScript, hovering,
      scrolling inside a nested container, opening a menu or signing in;
  (b) legible on mobile and desktop with contrast and size comparable to other
      footer text, and reachable by keyboard;
  (c) not hidden, clipped, obscured, removed after load, or styled to blend
      into the background.
You may place the credit below the fold in the normal footer. You may choose to
add rel="nofollow", rel="sponsored" or rel="ugc" to the link; the Licensor does
not require or prohibit link qualifiers. The link must point to
https://nextjsblog.com without passing through a redirect, interstitial or
tracking service that alters the destination. The supplied ProductCredit
component satisfies these requirements; an equivalent implementation is allowed.
Attribution is not required for private development, non-public previews,
non-HTML outputs such as feeds and APIs, or pages of a host website that are
not rendered by the Software.

